{{Term/Store|Fortified Pumpkin|Fortified Pumpkins|Series, BotW, TotK, AoC, AoI|plural}} are recurring [[Item]]s in {{TLoZ Series}}.<ref name="BotW Inventory"/><ref name="TotK Inventory"/><ref name="AoC Material"/><ref name="AoI Materials"/>

==Location and Uses==
==={{BotW|-}}===
{{Compendium/Extract|Fortified Pumpkin}}
Fortified Pumpkins are one of three foodstuffs favored by the [[Sheikah]], with the others being [[Swift Carrot]]s and [[Mighty Bananas]]. They are primarily and exclusively cultivated by the Sheikah farmer [[Olkin]], who sells 8 from his field in [[Kakariko Village]]. Olkin sells the Fortified Pumpkins he grows from [[Olkin's Pumpkins]] because his rival, [[Steen]], refuses to have them stocked at his [[Trissa|wife]]'s [[High Spirits Produce|shop]]. There are nine [[Pumpkin]] plants in the patch, yet only eight bear fruit. During the evening, Olkin's wife [[Mellie]] [[Cooking|Cooks]] him dishes containing many Fortified Pumpkins,<ref name="BotW Olkin"/> which Olkin feels is better than [[Swift Carrot]]s.<ref name="BotW Olkin 2"/> Some may also be purchased from the [[Wandering Merchant]] [[Cambo]], and [[Hinox]]es have a chance to drop them upon their defeat.

Eaten raw, Fortified Pumpkins restore half of a [[Heart]]. They can also be roasted by a [[Fire]] or [[Scorching Climate]] to create [[Baked Fortified Pumpkin]]s. When Cooked in a dish, the resulting [[Meal]] temporarily provides [[Link]] with [[Defense Up]].<ref name="BotW Inventory"/> At the [[Kochi Dye Shop]], Fortified Pumpkins can be used to create Orange [[Dye]].

As part of the [[Side Quest]] "[[Riddles of Hyrule]]", [[Walton]] will ask Link to bring him Kakariko Village's specialty [[Fruit]], which has rock-hard flesh.<ref name="BotW Walton"/> If Link returns with a Fortified Pumpkin, Walton will be excited he figured the riddle out and move on to the next one.<ref name="BotW Walton 2"/>

